Basic concept:
	POSIXy unless stated otherwise
	Microkernel servers, special files, other objects can be queried for what interfaces they support
	An interface is a UUID representing the OOP-style interface supported by an object or server
	Interfaces are used both within the same address space (where a tool can autogen code for it) and between spaces/processes

A simple userspace lib allows querying an object for an interface and returns the relevant C struct or a generic struct for invoking methods etc
If the object is within the same space, it goes direct, otherwise IPC magic happens
